[
 {
  "id": "F1",
  "file": "src/integrations/issue-queue.ts",
  "line": 117,
  "title": "Tie re-approval to the latest failure episode, judged only by timeline order",
  "detail": "Thank you: A, B and E are fixed, and review confirmed both migrations apply in order and match a single correct migration on populated databases. This is the last review round.\n\nThe re-approval guard compares the failure label's timestamp with the latest run's completion time. Suppose a retry is created after reconciliation and fails before the next poll. The previous run's `limitless:failed` label is still present, and the lifecycle (~src/integrations/issue-lifecycle.ts:196) doesn't re-apply it. If that label predates the latest failure's second, every later trusted approval is rejected forever. If both failures fall in the same second, rounding lets the earlier approval authorize another retry with no fresh approval. Both reproduced.\n\nFix:\n- When a run fails, make the failure a new labeled event even if the label is already present (remove it, then add it), and record which run that event belongs to.\n- Eligibility then uses only timeline order: re-approval needs a trusted priority label, present now, applied after the most recent `limitless:failed` labeled event. Drop the completion-time comparison.\n\nTest both reproduced cases."
 },
 {
  "id": "F2",
  "file": "src/integrations/issue-lifecycle.ts",
  "line": 137,
  "title": "Never advance the cursor past a task that didn't fit the remaining call budget",
  "detail": "The cursor advances before it's known whether a task can make progress. Behind 49 persistently failing calls, a task that needs two calls (an owner-comment check, or a label re-read plus write) gets only the last slot. The next poll starts after it and repeats the same pattern, so it starves indefinitely. Reproduced for labels and comments over ten polls while respecting the 50-call cap.\n\nFix: before starting a task, check that the remaining budget covers the calls it needs. If it doesn't, end the poll with the cursor on that task, so it runs first next poll with the full budget. A task that fails rotates to the back, as now."
 },
